      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "pd-cognitive-impairment-and-dementia-treatment",
      "documentConcept": "PD cognitive impairment and dementia treatment",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b",
      "text": "PD cognitive treatment depends on whether functional independence is preserved or cognition impairs daily activities. Rivastigmine has the strongest established drug evidence for PD dementia, with moderate benefits and tolerability trade-offs. Dementia drug results should not be generalized to PD-MCI. Cognitive training, stimulation and aerobic activity have different roles and evidence limits; durable prevention of cognitive decline remains unproven. Guideline recommendations for memantine and galantamine differ and require attribution to the issuing guideline and date.",
      "sources": [
