      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:715614474ca4cf683cb6b55611391f4f3c7aa73c96e073e7ce485313db65533b",
      "text": "Cognitive training has mixed evidence: the German guideline supports it for PD-MCI but notes small, heterogeneous trials; an eight-week computerized-training RCT in PD patients with subjective cognitive complaints found no benefit on primary planning accuracy and no group differences at follow-up. The populations and interventions differ, so this is a limitation on generalization rather than proof that every training program fails.",
